      "claim": "Imatinib, a lower-similarity analog, showed poor CNS penetration in a clinical CSF/plasma measurement (2.7%), providing a contradictory example that is outweighed by more similar positive evidence.",
      "evidence_role": "contradictory"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "moderate",
  "decision_summary": "The closest and several related analogs show direct evidence of BBB penetration via PET, Kp,uu, brain/plasma ratios, and CSF sampling, supporting a pass. Lower-similarity efflux-limited imatinib evidence is outweighed by the more structurally relevant positive records.",
